lesson_basics_capacities_short:
Three Capacities measure different aspect of your country's power.

@bur![Nbsp][concept_bureaucracy] is the extent of your government's bureaucratic reach.

@aut![Nbsp][concept_authority] is the ability of the [concept_head_of_state] to rule by decree.

@inf![Nbsp][concept_influence] lets you throw your weight around in world affairs.

lesson_basics_capacities_desc:
Three Capacities measure different aspect of your country's power.

@bur![Nbsp][concept_bureaucracy] is the extent of your government's bureaucratic reach.

@aut![Nbsp][concept_authority] is the ability of the [concept_head_of_state] to rule by decree.

@inf![Nbsp][concept_influence] lets you throw your weight around in world affairs.

Capacities originate from some [Concept('concept_government_building', '$concept_government_buildings$')], certain [Concept('concept_law', '$concept_laws$')], and your [concept_rank] respectively. You get to decide how to allocate them to further your interests.

Unspent Capacity will provide a minor boost to one aspect of your country, while overspending will incur a major penalty.

lesson_fix_capacity_deficit_how_5_desc:
Next we will take a look at @aut![Nbsp][concept_authority], so hover it to see its breakdown.

@aut![Nbsp]$concept_authority$ originates from [Concept('concept_law','$concept_laws$')], particularly less liberal ones.

It is allocated to levy [Concept('concept_consumption_tax','$concept_consumption_taxes$')] on [concept_pop_needs], impose your will on your [Concept('concept_pop','$concept_population$')] via [Concept('concept_decree','$concept_decrees$')], [concept_suppress] and [concept_bolster] [Concept('concept_interest_group','$concept_interest_groups$')], and similar actions.

lesson_fix_capacity_deficit_how_7_desc:
Finally let's hover @inf![Nbsp][concept_influence] to see its inflows and outflows.

@inf![Nbsp]$concept_influence$ originates primarily from your [concept_rank], which is a consequence of your relative [concept_prestige]. You can also earn @inf![Nbsp]$concept_influence$ from [Concept('concept_rivalry','$concept_rivalries$')], where each overlapping [concept_interest] earns you a small amount.

It is allocated to maintain [Concept('concept_diplomatic_pact','$concept_diplomatic_pacts$')], including [concept_subject] relationships. Influencing [Concept('concept_country','$concept_countries$')] of greater [concept_rank] often costs additional @inf!$concept_influence$.
